lawsuit over the  election before the state supreme court  oral arguments began this week you'll  remember anthony lost the district c  county commission race in november to  democrat ross miller  clark county commissioners first  suggested they would hold a special  election but then they  backed down from that the courts  expected to take several months before  issuing a ruling  battles over new voting rules in georgia  and other states has put congressional  legislation  at the forefront democrats are pushing  h.r 1 which they've dubbed the for the  people act  democrats say it would expand voter  access president joe biden is pushing  his party to get it to his desk  the i-team's david charns asked nevada  senator jackie rosen if she supports the  bill  before the people act we have you know  legislation here in nevada to expand  voting um we also have legislation that  is likely not going to pass because it  doesn't have the numbers to restrict  voting and then  nationally we have the for the people  act to you know solidify some of  voting rights what's your stance on that  right now my stance is this is that it  is a bedrock of our democracy  that every vote counts that we tell  everyone your voice is your vote  and so i want to be sure that everyone  has  equal access to the ballot box all  across america  this is not a democratic republican  issue this  is an american issue the world is  watching  and so there's been no evidence of voter  fraud we need to be sure  that we have equitable access to the  ballot box  everywhere so everyone who's eligible to  vote  has the right to make their voice heard  and the world is watching how we do that  is there anything in the bill that you  wouldn't support right now or you  i mean i know it's early but is there  something in it that you'd like to see  or you haven't seen  well you know what they're still working  on all the final languages between the  house and the senate version so we'll  we'll see what that actually comes down  to as people begin to discuss it  nevada's other democratic senator  catherine cortez masto  also supports the for the people act  republicans  oppose the bill senate minority leader  mitch mcconnell laid out why on march  25th  it would forcibly rewrite every state's  election laws in ways that  defy common sense and are deeply  unpopular with american voters it would  mandate nearly unrestricted same-day  registration  it would mandate big loopholes that  would render voter id  almost meaningless it would make every  state legalize ballot harvesting where  paid operatives can turn up carrying big  piles of ballots with other people's  names on them  is zero chain of custody  democrats want to hide behind the mantle  of voting rights what they're really  proposing is less security  less integrity and a grab bag of changes  that are deeply  deeply unpopular just look at the other  changes with zero relationship to voting  rights that democrats want to smuggle in  behind that smoke screen this bill would  take the federal election commission  from an evenly split bipartisan panel  to a partisan body so that democrats  could rule unilaterally  so far a vote on h.r 1 has not been  scheduled on capitol hill  coming up next on politics now we're  going to check in with our washington  d.c  bureau president joe biden announces a  set of executive actions  to curb gun violence and bazel john  reporting in washington  we have the latest on the announcement  as the weather warms up more americans  want to travel  and gather but will a vaccine passport  be necessary  i'll have the latest you're watching  politics now  this week president joe biden announced  a set of executive actions to curb gun  violence here in the u.s  washington dc correspondent basil john  reports on this latest announcement  gun violence in this country is an  epidemic  thursday president joe biden issued new  executive actions he says  will improve gun safety we have an  opportunity to fulfill the first  responsibility of government  to keep our people safe president  biden's actions  will create tighter regulations around  guns assembled from kits  and pistols with a stabilizing brace as  well as direct the justice department  to publish red flag legislation that can  be adapted by states  just like with background checks the  vast majority of the americans support  these  extreme risk protection order laws  it's time to put these laws on the books  and protect even more people  but republicans say this is not the  right way for the president to tackle  gun violence  he's not holding people accountable for  their actions  he's holding innocent people accountable  for the actions of people who are  violent pennsylvania republican  congressman fred keller says the  violence doesn't come from the guns  but from bad individuals you're not  going to solve that problem  until you get to the root cause and stop  talking about the instrument somebody  uses  and talk about what causes that behavior  keller says the issue should be left up  to congress  but the president says curbing gun  violence  requires taking action whether congress  acts or not  i'm going to use all the resources at my  disposal as president to keep the  american people safe  reporting in washington i'm basil john  bills with similar regulations are being  considered at the legislative session  here in nevada  assembly bill 286 bans those  home-assembled firearms kits the ghost  guns we just heard about  it's the second most commented bill so  far more than 2800 comments in fact 2400  against it  400 for it nevada also previously passed  a law allowing family members  household members and police to get a  court order seizing someone's gun for up  to a year  countries are beginning to implement  vaccine passports both for their own  citizens  and for tourists from other countries  the question is will america be next  some private industries are already  moving in that direction the travel  industry  supports the idea but governors in some  red states are saying no  most people want to travel and they  don't care if they have to show one more  id it's completely unacceptable for  either the government or the private  sector to impose upon you  the requirement that you show proof of  vaccine  plenty to talk about from washington dc  that's why we have alexander limon there  with  some of the headlines right now let's  start talking with  vaccine passports some areas have  already implemented them new york city  most notably what is the latest guidance  from the byte administration on putting  these in place  well we've heard from the white house a  couple times now on this issue and  they've been pretty consistent and  adamant as well in saying that it will  not be the federal government that  implements any type of mandate requiring  a vaccine passport or requiring  vaccination in general for people  to do different types of public  activities but they also say they do  recognize  like you mentioned that the private  sector maybe even states or cities  may implement some sort of vaccine  requirement or  vaccine passport requirement in order to  allow people to travel or to attend  really big  public events like sporting events and  so because they recognize it's  likely going to happen in one form or  another the white house does say they  will help  to develop a system that they say will  hopefully be  fair and accessible to everyone and also  safe to make sure you know that people's  personal safety information isn't being  jeopardized to hackers  or not at risk to be leaked out to the  public  in some places across the country  they're trying to mandate that you can't  have these vaccine passports what's  happening in some of the states across  the country  well in some states we're seeing  governors sign executive orders or new  laws that say  that any state agencies or tax funded  agencies cannot require  any type of vaccine passport or  vaccination proof  but in one state in florida the governor  there has actually gone a step further  and is requiring  that even private businesses not be  allowed to ask people to require proof  of vaccine  and that's going to be a little tricky  it'll be interesting to see whether or  not governor desantis can move forward  with that  because for example there's a lot of  international travel that happens in and  out of florida  whether it be by air or cruise ships  that go to  places that are now starting to require  that tourists  have vaccine passports places like  iceland and greece for example  and that was alex limon from washington  dc you're watching  politics now  congressional delegation has been in  southern nevada this week pitching the  american rescue plan  on thursday a group of democrats  gathered up in north las vegas at a food  bank there senators jackie rosen  catherine cortez masto  congresswoman susie lee and dina titus  and congressman steven horsford were all  there  taking part in the food bank  more videos are out from the government  investigation into  unidentified flying objects this was  revealed by  our own george knapp this week it shows  a group of flying  pyramids floating above a navy warship  the video clip is part of a briefing  prepared by the pentagon's  u-app task force which is working on a  comprehensive report  for congress about the ufo mystery if  you would like to learn more about this  and the pentagon's task force just head  over to mysterywire.com  you can check out the story there and a  whole lot more about  ufos and flying pyramids thank you very  much for watching politics now this week  you can stay up to date online of course  at 8newsnow.com  we're back with you next saturday with  the latest from carson city and  washington dc  take care  [Music]  you
 

